      "id": "sol.ahsme-1962-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(8=2^3\\) and \\(32=2^5,\\) the equation becomes \\(2^{3x}=2^5.\\) Hence \\(3x=5\\) and \\(x=\\frac{5}{3}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
